Aim
To write a Python program using Pandas to create a DataFrame containing student names and marks, and Matplotlib to represent the student marks using a bar chart.
Algorithm
1. Start the program.
2. Import the Pandas and Matplotlib libraries.
3. Create a dictionary containing student names and their marks.
4. Convert the dictionary into a Pandas DataFrame.
5. Display the student data.
6. Create a bar chart using student names and marks.
7. Add labels to the X-axis and Y-axis.
8. Add a title to the graph.
9. Display the bar chart using plt.show().
10. Stop the program.

Code:

import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
# Creating data
data = {
    "Name": ["Siya", "Riya", "Priya", "Anu"],
    "Marks": [90, 80, 95, 85]
}
df = pd.DataFrame(data)
# Display DataFrame
print("Student Data:")
print(df)
# Creating Bar Chart
plt.bar(df["Name"], df["Marks"])
# Adding labels and title
plt.xlabel("Student Name")
plt.ylabel("Marks")
plt.title("Student Marks Analysis")
# Display graph
plt.show()

